# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The visible edges of triangle meshes seen square onto a view plane: the
# projection a section draws beyond its cut and an elevation draws whole
# (drawing quality plan, item 15; docs/notes/section-projection.md).
#
# Drawing coordinates are the view plane's: x along its x axis, y along its
# y axis, and depth along y axis x x axis, which for a section is the side
# its line looks to (`the bim section plane from … to …`). What lies before
# the plane (depth below 0) is left out; so is what lies beyond the view
# depth when the view has one.
#
# What it draws of a mesh: its edges where the surface folds (two faces at
# more than a degree whose shared corners carry different normals, or at
# more than 60 degrees whatever the normals say), its outline seen from the
# view (one face toward the viewer, the other not) and its open borders,
# each only when a face beside it looks toward the viewer. Coplanar
# triangles of one face, and the facets of a smoothly shaded curve, draw no
# line between them.
#
# Nor does a flush edge: one with a single face toward the viewer beside it
# (a border, or an outline or fold against faces turned away), where on the
# other side of the same line another face looks the same way in the same
# plane (within 0.1 mm and a quarter of a degree). That other face must be
# of the same mesh (a face whose triangulation has T-vertices, a sliver left
# out, a frame's touching rails and posts), or of a mesh showing the same
# finish (`finishes`: two walls of one material stacked flush on two
# storeys). Faces of different finishes, or of meshes without one, keep the
# joint between them; an outline against the background, a true fold and a
# reveal have no such face beyond them and stay. The one-sided edges are
# hashed by their line (angle and offset in the drawing) and their depth
# (bins of 250 mm), so each finds its partners among the few on nearly the
# same line in space, not among every edge the drawing shows on that line.
#
# Hidden-line removal is exact for triangles, not a painter's guess: each
# edge is cut against every triangle in front of it that its projection
# crosses (triangles found through a grid over the drawing), and the part
# lying behind a triangle's plane is taken away; so are the parts behind
# the view's cut polygons, which stand on the plane at depth 0. The meshes
# are what the 3D view tessellates, so a curved element is as exact as its
# facets.
import views/drawings/bim_drawing.dl
import bim/bim_index.dl

# One mesh to project: the element it belongs to, its triangles in model
# coordinates, and whether its edges are drawn (`outlined`) or it only hides
# what lies behind it (a window's glass, a door's leaf). `finishes` names
# what its faces show (a material), and `faceFinishes` gives each triangle's
# finish as a position in `finishes` (all the first when it is empty); a
# mesh without finishes meets no other mesh flush (see the head of this
# file).
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim projection mesh record
    members:
        elementId as a 64 bit integer
        shape as a fast mesh record
        outlined as a boolean
        finishes as the type of (a cad topology list of a string)
        faceFinishes as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)

function a bim projection mesh of {a 64 bit integer:elementId} shaped {fast mesh record:meshShape} outlined {boolean:drawsEdges}:
    execute:
        return @intrinsic("construct", a bim projection mesh record, elementId, meshShape, drawsEdges, a cad topology list of a string, a cad topology list of an integer)

# The same mesh with every face showing `finishName`.
function a bim projection mesh of {a 64 bit integer:elementId} shaped {fast mesh record:meshShape} outlined {boolean:drawsEdges} finished {a string:finishName}:
    execute:
        set made to a bim projection mesh of elementId shaped meshShape outlined drawsEdges
        append finishName to (made's finishes's values)
        return made

# The finish face `triangleIndex` of `meshEntry` shows; empty when the mesh
# names none.
function the bim finish of face {integer:triangleIndex} in {bim projection mesh record:meshEntry}:
    execute:
        set finishNames to meshEntry's finishes's values
        if (the length of finishNames) = 0:
            return the string form of ""
        set finishSlot to 0
        if triangleIndex < (the length of (meshEntry's faceFinishes's values)):
            set finishSlot to the item at triangleIndex in (meshEntry's faceFinishes's values)
        if (finishSlot < 0) or (finishSlot >= (the length of finishNames)):
            return the string form of ""
        return the item at finishSlot in finishNames

# A visible piece of an edge, in drawing coordinates, with its depth at its
# middle.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim projected edge record
    members:
        elementId as a 64 bit integer
        start as a cad vector2
        finish as a cad vector2
        depth as a 64 bit floating-point number

# An edge the projection draws unless it is flush, in drawing coordinates
# and depth. A `oneSided` edge has exactly one face beside it that looks
# toward the viewer: its border, or its outline or fold against faces
# turned away. For such an edge `normal` is that face's normal, `inward`
# the direction in its plane from the edge into it, and `meshNumber` and
# `finishName` its mesh and finish; only a one-sided edge can be flush.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim projection stroke record
    members:
        elementId as a 64 bit integer
        fromCorner as a cad vector3
        toCorner as a cad vector3
        oneSided as a boolean
        meshNumber as an integer
        finishName as a string
        normal as a cad vector3
        inward as a cad vector3

# The triangles that hide edges, in drawing coordinates (x along, y up,
# z depth), three corners each, turned anticlockwise in the drawing, and a
# grid of `columns` by `rows` cells over them: cell c holds the triangles
# `cellItems` lists from `cellStarts` c to c + 1. `seen` marks the triangles
# an edge has met already.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim projection occluders record
    members:
        corners as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector3)
        lows as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector2)
        highs as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector2)
        nearest as the type of (a cad topology list of a 64 bit floating-point number)
        gridLow as a cad vector2
        cellWidth as a 64 bit floating-point number
        cellHeight as a 64 bit floating-point number
        columns as an integer
        rows as an integer
        cellStarts as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        cellItems as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        seen as the type of (a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer)

# How far behind a triangle's plane a point must lie to be hidden by it
# (metres), and how far outside its outline a point may lie and still be
# hidden (metres), so that the triangles of one face leave no gap.
local function the bim projection depth tolerance:
    replacement:
        0.0001
local function the bim projection edge tolerance:
    replacement:
        0.0000001

# The shortest visible piece kept, in metres in the drawing.
local function the bim projection shortest piece:
    replacement:
        0.0001

# 2 to the 21st: the room a welded vertex number and a triangle number each
# take in a sorting key.
local function the bim projection key room:
    replacement:
        2097152

# Flush edges (see the head of this file): how far a point of one edge may
# lie off the other's line (metres), how near the faces' normals must be
# (the cosine of about a quarter of a degree), and the bins of the line
# hash: an angle in radians, an offset from the hash's origin (`the bim
# flush origin of`) in metres, and a depth in metres.
local function the bim flush tolerance:
    replacement:
        0.0001
local function the bim flush alignment:
    replacement:
        0.99999
local function the bim flush angle bin:
    replacement:
        0.0001
local function the bim flush offset bin:
    replacement:
        0.001
local function the bim flush depth bin:
    replacement:
        0.25
# The most depth bins an edge is keyed in; an edge reaching through more
# (one running steeply into the depth) is keyed once, in the deep bin,
# which every edge searches.
local function the bim flush depth reach:
    replacement:
        32
local function the bim flush deep bin:
    replacement:
        1099511627776
# The grid (metres) the flush hash's origin is rounded to (`the bim flush
# origin of`): coarse, so that an edit seldom moves it, and fine
# enough to keep it near the model.
local function the bim flush origin grid:
    replacement:
        64.0
# 2 to the 25th: the room an offset bin takes in a line key; offsets are
# counted from half of it, so lines up to 16 km from the hash's origin are
# keyed apart.
local function the bim flush offset room:
    replacement:
        33554432
# 2 to the 16th: the room the hash of an angle bin and a depth bin takes in
# a line key; times the offset room and the key room it stays below 2 to
# the 62nd.
local function the bim flush hash room:
    replacement:
        65536

local function the bim depth axis of {cad plane:viewPlane}:
    execute:
        set upAxis to viewPlane's yAxis
        set alongAxis to viewPlane's xAxis
        return a cad vector3 with x ((upAxis's y * alongAxis's z) - (upAxis's z * alongAxis's y)), y ((upAxis's z * alongAxis's x) - (upAxis's x * alongAxis's z)) and z ((upAxis's x * alongAxis's y) - (upAxis's y * alongAxis's x))

# Model point `location` in drawing coordinates and depth.
local function the bim view coordinates of {cad vector3:location} on {cad plane:viewPlane} deep along {cad vector3:depthAxis}:
    execute:
        set offset to the cad difference of location and viewPlane's origin
        return a cad vector3 with x (the cad dot of offset and viewPlane's xAxis), y (the cad dot of offset and viewPlane's yAxis) and z (the cad dot of offset and depthAxis)

# A direction `heading` in drawing coordinates and depth.
local function the bim view direction of {cad vector3:heading} on {cad plane:viewPlane} deep along {cad vector3:depthAxis}:
    execute:
        return a cad vector3 with x (the cad dot of heading and viewPlane's xAxis), y (the cad dot of heading and viewPlane's yAxis) and z (the cad dot of heading and depthAxis)

# The corners of polygon `polygonCorners` (drawing coordinates and depth)
# on the side of depth `bound` that `sideSign` names (1 beyond it, -1
# before it), the polygon cut where it crosses.
local function append bim corners in {a pointer to a list:polygonCorners} kept {a 64 bit floating-point number:sideSign} of depth {a 64 bit floating-point number:bound} into {a pointer to a list:keptCorners}:
    execute:
        set cornerCount to the length of polygonCorners
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to cornerCount:
            set here to the item at cornerCursor in polygonCorners
            set there to the item at (the remainder of (cornerCursor + 1) divided by cornerCount) in polygonCorners
            set hereSide to sideSign * (here's z - bound)
            set thereSide to sideSign * (there's z - bound)
            if hereSide >= 0.0:
                append here to keptCorners
            if ((hereSide >= 0.0) and (thereSide < 0.0)) or ((hereSide < 0.0) and (thereSide >= 0.0)):
                set fraction to hereSide / (hereSide - thereSide)
                append (a cad vector3 with x (here's x + ((there's x - here's x) * fraction)), y (here's y + ((there's y - here's y) * fraction)) and z (here's z + ((there's z - here's z) * fraction))) to keptCorners

# Triangle `firstCorner`, `secondCorner`, `thirdCorner` (drawing
# coordinates and depth) as an occluder: turned anticlockwise, unless it
# stands edge-on to the view.
local function add bim occluder {cad vector3:firstCorner}, {cad vector3:secondCorner} and {cad vector3:thirdCorner} to {bim projection occluders record:occluders}:
    execute:
        set twiceArea to ((secondCorner's x - firstCorner's x) * (thirdCorner's y - firstCorner's y)) - ((thirdCorner's x - firstCorner's x) * (secondCorner's y - firstCorner's y))
        if (the absolute value of twiceArea) < 0.000000000001:
            return nothing
        append firstCorner to (occluders's corners's values)
        if twiceArea > 0.0:
            append secondCorner to (occluders's corners's values)
            append thirdCorner to (occluders's corners's values)
        else:
            append thirdCorner to (occluders's corners's values)
            append secondCorner to (occluders's corners's values)
        append (a cad vector2 with x (the minimum of firstCorner's x and (the minimum of secondCorner's x and thirdCorner's x)) and y (the minimum of firstCorner's y and (the minimum of secondCorner's y and thirdCorner's y))) to (occluders's lows's values)
        append (a cad vector2 with x (the maximum of firstCorner's x and (the maximum of secondCorner's x and thirdCorner's x)) and y (the maximum of firstCorner's y and (the maximum of secondCorner's y and thirdCorner's y))) to (occluders's highs's values)
        append (the minimum of firstCorner's z and (the minimum of secondCorner's z and thirdCorner's z)) to (occluders's nearest's values)

# The triangles of a mesh whose corners are `viewCorners` (drawing
# coordinates and depth) as occluders, each cut to the depths from 0 to
# `farDepth`, those wholly outside the drawing's width from `lowAlong` to
# `highAlong` left out.
local function add bim occluders of {fast mesh record:meshShape} at {a pointer to a list:viewCorners} offset {integer:cornerOffset} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowAlong} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:highAlong} until {a 64 bit floating-point number:farDepth} into {bim projection occluders record:occluderSet}:
    execute:
        set indices to meshShape's triangles's values
        set triangleCount to (the length of indices) / 3
        loop triangleCursor from 0 to triangleCount:
            set firstCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + (the item at (triangleCursor * 3) in indices)) in viewCorners
            set secondCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + (the item at ((triangleCursor * 3) + 1) in indices)) in viewCorners
            set thirdCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + (the item at ((triangleCursor * 3) + 2) in indices)) in viewCorners
            set leastAlong to the minimum of firstCorner's x and (the minimum of secondCorner's x and thirdCorner's x)
            set mostAlong to the maximum of firstCorner's x and (the maximum of secondCorner's x and thirdCorner's x)
            set leastDepth to the minimum of firstCorner's z and (the minimum of secondCorner's z and thirdCorner's z)
            set mostDepth to the maximum of firstCorner's z and (the maximum of secondCorner's z and thirdCorner's z)
            set inWidth to (mostAlong >= lowAlong) and (leastAlong <= highAlong)
            set inDepth to (mostDepth >= 0.0) and (leastDepth <= farDepth)
            if inWidth and inDepth:
                if (leastDepth >= 0.0) and (mostDepth <= farDepth):
                    add bim occluder firstCorner, secondCorner and thirdCorner to occluderSet
                else:
                    set whole to an empty list of a cad vector3
                    append firstCorner to whole
                    append secondCorner to whole
                    append thirdCorner to whole
                    set beyondPlane to an empty list of a cad vector3
                    append bim corners in whole kept 1.0 of depth 0.0 into beyondPlane
                    set withinDepth to an empty list of a cad vector3
                    if (the length of beyondPlane) >= 3:
                        append bim corners in beyondPlane kept (0.0 - 1.0) of depth farDepth into withinDepth
                    if (the length of withinDepth) >= 3:
                        loop fanCursor from 1 to ((the length of withinDepth) - 1):
                            add bim occluder (the item at 0 in withinDepth), (the item at fanCursor in withinDepth) and (the item at (fanCursor + 1) in withinDepth) to occluderSet
                    free whole
                    free beyondPlane
                    free withinDepth

local function the bim grid column of {a 64 bit floating-point number:coordinate} in {bim projection occluders record:occluders}:
    execute:
        set cell to (the floor of ((coordinate - occluders's gridLow's x) / occluders's cellWidth)) as an integer
        if cell < 0:
            return 0
        if cell >= occluders's columns:
            return occluders's columns - 1
        return cell

local function the bim grid row of {a 64 bit floating-point number:coordinate} in {bim projection occluders record:occluders}:
    execute:
        set cell to (the floor of ((coordinate - occluders's gridLow's y) / occluders's cellHeight)) as an integer
        if cell < 0:
            return 0
        if cell >= occluders's rows:
            return occluders's rows - 1
        return cell

# The grid over the occluders: about one cell per triangle, at most 128 by
# 128 cells, each triangle listed in every cell its box touches.
local function index bim occluders {a pointer to a bim projection occluders record:occluderSet}:
    execute:
        set triangleCount to the length of (occluderSet's lows's values)
        set lowX to 1e300
        set lowY to 1e300
        set highX to -1e300
        set highY to -1e300
        loop triangleCursor from 0 to triangleCount:
            set boxLow to the item at triangleCursor in (occluderSet's lows's values)
            set boxHigh to the item at triangleCursor in (occluderSet's highs's values)
            set lowX to the minimum of lowX and boxLow's x
            set lowY to the minimum of lowY and boxLow's y
            set highX to the maximum of highX and boxHigh's x
            set highY to the maximum of highY and boxHigh's y
        set gridSide to 1
        loop while ((gridSide * gridSide) < triangleCount) and (gridSide < 128):
            set gridSide to gridSide + 1
        set occluderSet's columns to gridSide
        set occluderSet's rows to gridSide
        if highX < lowX:
            set lowX to 0.0
            set lowY to 0.0
            set highX to 1.0
            set highY to 1.0
        set occluderSet's gridLow to a cad vector2 with x lowX and y lowY
        set occluderSet's cellWidth to (the maximum of (highX - lowX) and 0.001) / (gridSide as a 64 bit floating-point number)
        set occluderSet's cellHeight to (the maximum of (highY - lowY) and 0.001) / (gridSide as a 64 bit floating-point number)
        set cellCount to gridSide * gridSide
        set counts to an empty list of an integer
        loop cellCursor from 0 to (cellCount + 1):
            append 0 to counts
        loop triangleCursor from 0 to triangleCount:
            set boxLow to the item at triangleCursor in (occluderSet's lows's values)
            set boxHigh to the item at triangleCursor in (occluderSet's highs's values)
            set firstColumn to the bim grid column of boxLow's x in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            set lastColumn to the bim grid column of boxHigh's x in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            set firstRow to the bim grid row of boxLow's y in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            set lastRow to the bim grid row of boxHigh's y in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            loop rowCursor from firstRow to (lastRow + 1):
                loop columnCursor from firstColumn to (lastColumn + 1):
                    set cellIndex to (rowCursor * gridSide) + columnCursor
                    replace item at index (cellIndex + 1) in counts with ((the item at (cellIndex + 1) in counts) + 1)
        loop cellCursor from 0 to cellCount:
            replace item at index (cellCursor + 1) in counts with ((the item at (cellCursor + 1) in counts) + (the item at cellCursor in counts))
        loop cellCursor from 0 to (cellCount + 1):
            append (the item at cellCursor in counts) to (occluderSet's cellStarts's values)
        loop itemCursor from 0 to (the item at cellCount in counts):
            append 0 to (occluderSet's cellItems's values)
        loop triangleCursor from 0 to triangleCount:
            set boxLow to the item at triangleCursor in (occluderSet's lows's values)
            set boxHigh to the item at triangleCursor in (occluderSet's highs's values)
            set firstColumn to the bim grid column of boxLow's x in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            set lastColumn to the bim grid column of boxHigh's x in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            set firstRow to the bim grid row of boxLow's y in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            set lastRow to the bim grid row of boxHigh's y in (@intrinsic("dereference", occluderSet))
            loop rowCursor from firstRow to (lastRow + 1):
                loop columnCursor from firstColumn to (lastColumn + 1):
                    set cellIndex to (rowCursor * gridSide) + columnCursor
                    set slot to the item at cellIndex in counts
                    replace item at index slot in (occluderSet's cellItems's values) with triangleCursor
                    replace item at index cellIndex in counts with (slot + 1)
            append ((-1) as a 64 bit integer) to (occluderSet's seen's values)
        free counts

# What remains of the pieces `pieceStarts` to `pieceEnds` (parameters along
# an edge) once the stretch from `hiddenStart` to `hiddenEnd` is taken out.
local function take bim stretch {a 64 bit floating-point number:hiddenStart} until {a 64 bit floating-point number:hiddenEnd} out of {a pointer to a list:pieceStarts} and {a pointer to a list:pieceEnds}:
    execute:
        if hiddenEnd <= hiddenStart:
            return nothing
        set keptStarts to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        set keptEnds to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        loop pieceCursor from 0 to the length of pieceStarts:
            set pieceStart to the item at pieceCursor in pieceStarts
            set pieceEnd to the item at pieceCursor in pieceEnds
            if (hiddenEnd <= pieceStart) or (hiddenStart >= pieceEnd):
                append pieceStart to keptStarts
                append pieceEnd to keptEnds
            else:
                if hiddenStart > pieceStart:
                    append pieceStart to keptStarts
                    append hiddenStart to keptEnds
                if hiddenEnd < pieceEnd:
                    append hiddenEnd to keptStarts
                    append pieceEnd to keptEnds
        clear pieceStarts
        clear pieceEnds
        loop pieceCursor from 0 to the length of keptStarts:
            append (the item at pieceCursor in keptStarts) to pieceStarts
            append (the item at pieceCursor in keptEnds) to pieceEnds
        free keptStarts
        free keptEnds

# Whether drawing point `testedSpot` lies inside the cut polygons `polygons`
# (even-odd over all their loops) or within a hair of one of their edges.
local function bim spot {cad vector2:testedSpot} lies in cut {a pointer to a list:polygons}:
    execute:
        set inside to false
        set onEdge to false
        loop polygonCursor from 0 to the length of polygons:
            set ring to (the item at polygonCursor in polygons)'s points's values
            set cornerCount to the length of ring
            loop cornerCursor from 0 to cornerCount:
                set here to the item at cornerCursor in ring
                set there to the item at (the remainder of (cornerCursor + 1) divided by cornerCount) in ring
                if ((here's y > testedSpot's y) and (there's y <= testedSpot's y)) or ((here's y <= testedSpot's y) and (there's y > testedSpot's y)):
                    set crossX to here's x + (((testedSpot's y - here's y) / (there's y - here's y)) * (there's x - here's x))
                    if crossX > testedSpot's x:
                        set inside to inside = false
                set edgeX to there's x - here's x
                set edgeY to there's y - here's y
                set edgeSquare to (edgeX * edgeX) + (edgeY * edgeY)
                if edgeSquare > 0.0:
                    set fraction to (((testedSpot's x - here's x) * edgeX) + ((testedSpot's y - here's y) * edgeY)) / edgeSquare
                    set fraction to the maximum of 0.0 and (the minimum of 1.0 and fraction)
                    set nearX to (here's x + (fraction * edgeX)) - testedSpot's x
                    set nearY to (here's y + (fraction * edgeY)) - testedSpot's y
                    if ((nearX * nearX) + (nearY * nearY)) < 0.000000000001:
                        set onEdge to true
        return inside or onEdge

# Takes out of the pieces of the edge from `edgeStart` to `edgeEnd`
# (drawing coordinates) what the cut polygons of `cutSource` cover.
local function take bim cut {bim cut source record:cutSource} out of edge {cad vector2:edgeStart} to {cad vector2:edgeEnd} from {a pointer to a list:pieceStarts} and {a pointer to a list:pieceEnds}:
    execute:
        set polygons to cutSource's polygons's values
        set crossings to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        append 0.0 to crossings
        set runX to edgeEnd's x - edgeStart's x
        set runY to edgeEnd's y - edgeStart's y
        set touching to false
        loop polygonCursor from 0 to the length of polygons:
            set ring to (the item at polygonCursor in polygons)'s points's values
            set cornerCount to the length of ring
            loop cornerCursor from 0 to cornerCount:
                set here to the item at cornerCursor in ring
                set there to the item at (the remainder of (cornerCursor + 1) divided by cornerCount) in ring
                set sideX to there's x - here's x
                set sideY to there's y - here's y
                set denominator to (runX * sideY) - (runY * sideX)
                if (the absolute value of denominator) > 0.000000000001:
                    set startX to here's x - edgeStart's x
                    set startY to here's y - edgeStart's y
                    set alongParameter to ((startX * sideY) - (startY * sideX)) / denominator
                    set acrossParameter to ((startX * runY) - (startY * runX)) / denominator
                    if (((alongParameter > 0.0) and (alongParameter < 1.0)) and (acrossParameter >= -0.000001)) and (acrossParameter <= 1.000001):
                        append alongParameter to crossings
                        set touching to true
        append 1.0 to crossings
        # Sorted by insertion: an edge crosses a cut a few times at most.
        loop sortCursor from 1 to the length of crossings:
            set moving to the item at sortCursor in crossings
            set slot to sortCursor
            set shifting to true
            loop while shifting:
                if slot = 0:
                    set shifting to false
                else if (the item at (slot - 1) in crossings) > moving:
                    replace item at index slot in crossings with (the item at (slot - 1) in crossings)
                    set slot to slot - 1
                else:
                    set shifting to false
            replace item at index slot in crossings with moving
        loop crossingCursor from 0 to ((the length of crossings) - 1):
            set fromParameter to the item at crossingCursor in crossings
            set toParameter to the item at (crossingCursor + 1) in crossings
            if toParameter > fromParameter:
                set middle to (fromParameter + toParameter) * 0.5
                set middleSpot to a cad vector2 with x (edgeStart's x + (runX * middle)) and y (edgeStart's y + (runY * middle))
                if bim spot middleSpot lies in cut polygons:
                    take bim stretch fromParameter until toParameter out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds
        free crossings

# The parameters along the edge from `edgeStart` to `edgeEnd` (drawing
# coordinates and depth) that triangle `triangleIndex` hides, taken out of
# the pieces.
local function take bim triangle {integer:triangleIndex} among {bim projection occluders record:occluders} out of edge {cad vector3:edgeStart} to {cad vector3:edgeEnd} from {a pointer to a list:pieceStarts} and {a pointer to a list:pieceEnds}:
    execute:
        set cornerA to the item at (triangleIndex * 3) in (occluders's corners's values)
        set cornerB to the item at ((triangleIndex * 3) + 1) in (occluders's corners's values)
        set cornerC to the item at ((triangleIndex * 3) + 2) in (occluders's corners's values)
        set enter to 0.0
        set leave to 1.0
        set runX to edgeEnd's x - edgeStart's x
        set runY to edgeEnd's y - edgeStart's y
        set tolerance to the bim projection edge tolerance
        loop sideCursor from 0 to 3:
            set sideFrom to cornerA
            set sideTo to cornerB
            if sideCursor = 1:
                set sideFrom to cornerB
                set sideTo to cornerC
            if sideCursor = 2:
                set sideFrom to cornerC
                set sideTo to cornerA
            set sideX to sideTo's x - sideFrom's x
            set sideY to sideTo's y - sideFrom's y
            set sideLength to the square root of ((sideX * sideX) + (sideY * sideY))
            # The inward normal of an anticlockwise side, of unit length.
            set inwardX to (0.0 - sideY) / sideLength
            set inwardY to sideX / sideLength
            set atStart to ((edgeStart's x - sideFrom's x) * inwardX) + ((edgeStart's y - sideFrom's y) * inwardY)
            set change to (runX * inwardX) + (runY * inwardY)
            if (the absolute value of change) < 0.000000000000001:
                if atStart < (0.0 - tolerance):
                    set leave to -1.0
            else:
                set crossing to ((0.0 - tolerance) - atStart) / change
                if change > 0.0:
                    set enter to the maximum of enter and crossing
                else:
                    set leave to the minimum of leave and crossing
        if leave <= (enter + 0.000000000001):
            return nothing
        # The triangle's plane: depth = depthAt + slopeX (x - ax) + slopeY (y - ay).
        set twiceArea to ((cornerB's x - cornerA's x) * (cornerC's y - cornerA's y)) - ((cornerC's x - cornerA's x) * (cornerB's y - cornerA's y))
        set slopeX to (((cornerB's z - cornerA's z) * (cornerC's y - cornerA's y)) - ((cornerC's z - cornerA's z) * (cornerB's y - cornerA's y))) / twiceArea
        set slopeY to (((cornerB's x - cornerA's x) * (cornerC's z - cornerA's z)) - ((cornerC's x - cornerA's x) * (cornerB's z - cornerA's z))) / twiceArea
        set enterX to edgeStart's x + (runX * enter)
        set enterY to edgeStart's y + (runY * enter)
        set leaveX to edgeStart's x + (runX * leave)
        set leaveY to edgeStart's y + (runY * leave)
        set planeEnter to (cornerA's z + (slopeX * (enterX - cornerA's x))) + (slopeY * (enterY - cornerA's y))
        set planeLeave to (cornerA's z + (slopeX * (leaveX - cornerA's x))) + (slopeY * (leaveY - cornerA's y))
        set edgeEnter to edgeStart's z + ((edgeEnd's z - edgeStart's z) * enter)
        set edgeLeave to edgeStart's z + ((edgeEnd's z - edgeStart's z) * leave)
        set behindEnter to (edgeEnter - planeEnter) - (the bim projection depth tolerance)
        set behindLeave to (edgeLeave - planeLeave) - (the bim projection depth tolerance)
        if (behindEnter > 0.0) and (behindLeave > 0.0):
            take bim stretch enter until leave out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds
        else if (behindEnter > 0.0) or (behindLeave > 0.0):
            set turning to enter + ((leave - enter) * (behindEnter / (behindEnter - behindLeave)))
            if behindEnter > 0.0:
                take bim stretch enter until turning out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds
            else:
                take bim stretch turning until leave out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds

# The visible pieces of the edge from `edgeStart` to `edgeEnd` (drawing
# coordinates and depth) of element `elementId`, cut to the drawing's width
# and depth, appended to `found`. `edgeNumber` marks the triangles met.
local function append bim visible pieces of edge {cad vector3:edgeStart} till {cad vector3:edgeEnd} for element {a 64 bit integer:elementId} numbered {a 64 bit integer:edgeNumber} between {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowAlong} and {a 64 bit floating-point number:highAlong} until {a 64 bit floating-point number:farDepth} among {bim projection occluders record:occluders} behind {bim view record:cutView} into {a pointer to a list:foundPieces}:
    execute:
        set enter to 0.0
        set leave to 1.0
        # Cut to depths 0 to `farDepth` and the width `lowAlong` to `highAlong`.
        loop limitCursor from 0 to 4:
            set atStart to edgeStart's z
            set atEnd to edgeEnd's z
            set bound to 0.0
            set sideSign to 1.0
            if limitCursor = 1:
                set bound to farDepth
                set sideSign to -1.0
            if limitCursor >= 2:
                set atStart to edgeStart's x
                set atEnd to edgeEnd's x
                set bound to lowAlong
            if limitCursor = 3:
                set bound to highAlong
                set sideSign to -1.0
            set fromStart to sideSign * (atStart - bound)
            set fromEnd to sideSign * (atEnd - bound)
            if (fromStart < 0.0) and (fromEnd < 0.0):
                set leave to -1.0
            else if (fromStart < 0.0) or (fromEnd < 0.0):
                set crossing to fromStart / (fromStart - fromEnd)
                if fromStart < 0.0:
                    set enter to the maximum of enter and crossing
                else:
                    set leave to the minimum of leave and crossing
        if leave <= enter:
            return nothing
        set runX to edgeEnd's x - edgeStart's x
        set runY to edgeEnd's y - edgeStart's y
        set runZ to edgeEnd's z - edgeStart's z
        set flatLength to the square root of ((runX * runX) + (runY * runY))
        if (flatLength * (leave - enter)) < (the bim projection shortest piece):
            return nothing
        set pieceStarts to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        set pieceEnds to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        append enter to pieceStarts
        append leave to pieceEnds
        set clippedStart to a cad vector3 with x (edgeStart's x + (runX * enter)), y (edgeStart's y + (runY * enter)) and z (edgeStart's z + (runZ * enter))
        set clippedEnd to a cad vector3 with x (edgeStart's x + (runX * leave)), y (edgeStart's y + (runY * leave)) and z (edgeStart's z + (runZ * leave))
        set boxLow to a cad vector2 with x (the minimum of clippedStart's x and clippedEnd's x) and y (the minimum of clippedStart's y and clippedEnd's y)
        set boxHigh to a cad vector2 with x (the maximum of clippedStart's x and clippedEnd's x) and y (the maximum of clippedStart's y and clippedEnd's y)
        set deepest to the maximum of clippedStart's z and clippedEnd's z
        # The triangles in the cells the edge's box touches.
        if (the length of (occluders's lows's values)) > 0:
            set firstColumn to the bim grid column of boxLow's x in occluders
            set lastColumn to the bim grid column of boxHigh's x in occluders
            set firstRow to the bim grid row of boxLow's y in occluders
            set lastRow to the bim grid row of boxHigh's y in occluders
            loop rowCursor from firstRow to (lastRow + 1):
                loop columnCursor from firstColumn to (lastColumn + 1):
                    set cellIndex to (rowCursor * occluders's columns) + columnCursor
                    set itemFrom to the item at cellIndex in (occluders's cellStarts's values)
                    set itemTo to the item at (cellIndex + 1) in (occluders's cellStarts's values)
                    loop itemCursor from itemFrom to itemTo:
                        set triangleIndex to the item at itemCursor in (occluders's cellItems's values)
                        if (the item at triangleIndex in (occluders's seen's values)) != edgeNumber:
                            replace item at index triangleIndex in (occluders's seen's values) with edgeNumber
                            set triangleLow to the item at triangleIndex in (occluders's lows's values)
                            set triangleHigh to the item at triangleIndex in (occluders's highs's values)
                            set overlapping to ((triangleLow's x <= boxHigh's x) and (triangleHigh's x >= boxLow's x)) and ((triangleLow's y <= boxHigh's y) and (triangleHigh's y >= boxLow's y))
                            set nearer to (the item at triangleIndex in (occluders's nearest's values)) < (deepest - (the bim projection depth tolerance))
                            if overlapping and nearer:
                                if (the length of pieceStarts) > 0:
                                    take bim triangle triangleIndex among occluders out of edge edgeStart to edgeEnd from pieceStarts and pieceEnds
        # The cut, which stands on the plane in front of everything beyond.
        set flatStart to a cad vector2 with x edgeStart's x and y edgeStart's y
        set flatEnd to a cad vector2 with x edgeEnd's x and y edgeEnd's y
        loop sourceCursor from 0 to the length of (cutView's sources's values):
            set cutSource to the item at sourceCursor in (cutView's sources's values)
            if (the length of pieceStarts) > 0:
                take bim cut cutSource out of edge flatStart to flatEnd from pieceStarts and pieceEnds
        loop pieceCursor from 0 to the length of pieceStarts:
            set pieceStart to the item at pieceCursor in pieceStarts
            set pieceEnd to the item at pieceCursor in pieceEnds
            if (flatLength * (pieceEnd - pieceStart)) >= (the bim projection shortest piece):
                set middle to (pieceStart + pieceEnd) * 0.5
                set startPoint to a cad vector2 with x (edgeStart's x + (runX * pieceStart)) and y (edgeStart's y + (runY * pieceStart))
                set endPoint to a cad vector2 with x (edgeStart's x + (runX * pieceEnd)) and y (edgeStart's y + (runY * pieceEnd))
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim projected edge record, elementId, startPoint, endPoint, edgeStart's z + (runZ * middle))) to foundPieces
        free pieceStarts
        free pieceEnds

# The position of `wanted` in the ascending `sortedKeys`, which holds it.
local function the bim key slot of {a 64 bit integer:wanted} among {a pointer to a list:sortedKeys}:
    execute:
        set lowSlot to 0
        set highSlot to the length of sortedKeys
        loop while (highSlot - lowSlot) > 1:
            set middleSlot to (lowSlot + highSlot) / 2
            if (the item at middleSlot in sortedKeys) <= wanted:
                set lowSlot to middleSlot
            else:
                set highSlot to middleSlot
        return lowSlot

# The model normal stored at corner `cornerIndex` of `meshShape`, in
# drawing coordinates and depth; zero when the mesh stores none.
local function the bim stored normal {integer:cornerIndex} of {fast mesh record:meshShape} on {cad plane:viewPlane} deep along {cad vector3:depthAxis}:
    execute:
        if cornerIndex >= (the length of (meshShape's normals's values)):
            return a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
        return the bim view direction of (the item at cornerIndex in (meshShape's normals's values)) on viewPlane deep along depthAxis

# The corner of triangle `triangleIndex` of `meshShape` welded to vertex
# `welded`, by `weldOf` (one welded vertex per corner).
local function the bim corner of triangle {integer:triangleIndex} in {fast mesh record:meshShape} welded to {integer:weldNumber} by {a pointer to a list:weldOf}:
    execute:
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to 3:
            set cornerIndex to the item at ((triangleIndex * 3) + cornerCursor) in (meshShape's triangles's values)
            if (the item at cornerIndex in weldOf) = weldNumber:
                return cornerIndex
        return the item at (triangleIndex * 3) in (meshShape's triangles's values)

# The unit direction in a face's plane square to its side from `fromCorner`
# to `toCorner`, toward `insideSpot` (a point of the face off that side);
# zero when they give none.
local function the bim flush inward from {cad vector3:fromCorner} to {cad vector3:toCorner} reaching {cad vector3:insideSpot}:
    execute:
        set zeroVector to a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
        set runVector to the cad difference of toCorner and fromCorner
        set runLength to the cad length of runVector
        if runLength <= 0.0:
            return zeroVector
        set unitRun to runVector scaled by (1.0 / runLength)
        set spotVector to the cad difference of insideSpot and fromCorner
        set acrossVector to the cad difference of spotVector and (unitRun scaled by (the cad dot of spotVector and unitRun))
        set acrossLength to the cad length of acrossVector
        if acrossLength <= 0.0:
            return zeroVector
        return acrossVector scaled by (1.0 / acrossLength)

# The unit direction in the plane of face `faceIndex` (corners `indices`
# from it times 3, in drawing coordinates in `viewCorners` from
# `cornerOffset`) square to its side from `fromCorner` to `toCorner`, into
# the face.
local function the bim flush inward of face {integer:faceIndex} among {a pointer to a list:indices} at {a pointer to a list:viewCorners} offset {integer:cornerOffset} from {cad vector3:fromCorner} to {cad vector3:toCorner}:
    execute:
        set firstSpot to the item at (cornerOffset + (the item at (faceIndex * 3) in indices)) in viewCorners
        set secondSpot to the item at (cornerOffset + (the item at ((faceIndex * 3) + 1) in indices)) in viewCorners
        set thirdSpot to the item at (cornerOffset + (the item at ((faceIndex * 3) + 2) in indices)) in viewCorners
        set middleSpot to a cad vector3 with x (((firstSpot's x + secondSpot's x) + thirdSpot's x) / 3.0), y (((firstSpot's y + secondSpot's y) + thirdSpot's y) / 3.0) and z (((firstSpot's z + secondSpot's z) + thirdSpot's z) / 3.0)
        return the bim flush inward from fromCorner to toCorner reaching middleSpot

# The edges of one outlined mesh, number `meshNumber`, that the projection
# draws unless they are flush (see the head of this file), appended to
# `candidateEdges`. Its `cornerCount` corners in drawing coordinates and
# depth are those of `viewCorners` from `cornerOffset`.
local function append bim drawn edges of {bim projection mesh record:meshEntry} numbered {integer:meshNumber} at {a pointer to a list:viewCorners} offset {integer:cornerOffset} counted {integer:cornerCount} on {cad plane:viewPlane} deep along {cad vector3:depthAxis} into {a pointer to a list:candidateEdges}:
    execute:
        set meshShape to meshEntry's shape
        set indices to meshShape's triangles's values
        set triangleCount to (the length of indices) / 3
        set keyRoom to (the bim projection key room) as a 64 bit integer
        if (cornerCount = 0) or (triangleCount = 0):
            return nothing
        if (cornerCount >= (the bim projection key room)) or (triangleCount >= (the bim projection key room)):
            return nothing
        # Weld corners that share a place: their keys on a grid of 1/2^20
        # of the mesh's largest extent (at least a micrometre).
        set lowCorner to the item at cornerOffset in viewCorners
        set highCorner to lowCorner
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to cornerCount:
            set viewCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + cornerCursor) in viewCorners
            set lowCorner to a cad vector3 with x (the minimum of lowCorner's x and viewCorner's x), y (the minimum of lowCorner's y and viewCorner's y) and z (the minimum of lowCorner's z and viewCorner's z)
            set highCorner to a cad vector3 with x (the maximum of highCorner's x and viewCorner's x), y (the maximum of highCorner's y and viewCorner's y) and z (the maximum of highCorner's z and viewCorner's z)
        set extent to the maximum of (highCorner's x - lowCorner's x) and (the maximum of (highCorner's y - lowCorner's y) and (highCorner's z - lowCorner's z))
        set quantum to the maximum of 0.000001 and (extent / 1048576.0)
        set cornerKeys to an empty list of a 64 bit integer
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to cornerCount:
            set viewCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + cornerCursor) in viewCorners
            set keyX to (the floor of (((viewCorner's x - lowCorner's x) / quantum) + 0.5)) as a 64 bit integer
            set keyY to (the floor of (((viewCorner's y - lowCorner's y) / quantum) + 0.5)) as a 64 bit integer
            set keyZ to (the floor of (((viewCorner's z - lowCorner's z) / quantum) + 0.5)) as a 64 bit integer
            append ((((keyX * keyRoom) + keyY) * keyRoom) + keyZ) to cornerKeys
        set sortedKeys to an empty list of a 64 bit integer
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to cornerCount:
            append (the item at cornerCursor in cornerKeys) to sortedKeys
        sort and deduplicate bim ids sortedKeys
        set weldOf to an empty list of an integer
        set weldedCorners to an empty list of a cad vector3
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to (the length of sortedKeys):
            append (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) to weldedCorners
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to cornerCount:
            set welded to the bim key slot of (the item at cornerCursor in cornerKeys) among sortedKeys
            append welded to weldOf
            replace item at index welded in weldedCorners with (the item at (cornerOffset + cornerCursor) in viewCorners)
        # Each triangle's normal, turned to agree with the normals the mesh
        # stores, and its sides keyed by their welded ends.
        set faceNormals to an empty list of a cad vector3
        set sideKeys to an empty list of a 64 bit integer
        loop triangleCursor from 0 to triangleCount:
            set firstIndex to the item at (triangleCursor * 3) in indices
            set secondIndex to the item at ((triangleCursor * 3) + 1) in indices
            set thirdIndex to the item at ((triangleCursor * 3) + 2) in indices
            set firstCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + firstIndex) in viewCorners
            set secondCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + secondIndex) in viewCorners
            set thirdCorner to the item at (cornerOffset + thirdIndex) in viewCorners
            set uX to secondCorner's x - firstCorner's x
            set uY to secondCorner's y - firstCorner's y
            set uZ to secondCorner's z - firstCorner's z
            set vX to thirdCorner's x - firstCorner's x
            set vY to thirdCorner's y - firstCorner's y
            set vZ to thirdCorner's z - firstCorner's z
            set normalX to (uY * vZ) - (uZ * vY)
            set normalY to (uZ * vX) - (uX * vZ)
            set normalZ to (uX * vY) - (uY * vX)
            set magnitude to the square root of (((normalX * normalX) + (normalY * normalY)) + (normalZ * normalZ))
            if magnitude > 0.0:
                set normalX to normalX / magnitude
                set normalY to normalY / magnitude
                set normalZ to normalZ / magnitude
            set storedSum to the cad sum of (the bim stored normal firstIndex of meshShape on viewPlane deep along depthAxis) and (the cad sum of (the bim stored normal secondIndex of meshShape on viewPlane deep along depthAxis) and (the bim stored normal thirdIndex of meshShape on viewPlane deep along depthAxis))
            if (((storedSum's x * normalX) + (storedSum's y * normalY)) + (storedSum's z * normalZ)) < 0.0:
                set normalX to 0.0 - normalX
                set normalY to 0.0 - normalY
                set normalZ to 0.0 - normalZ
            append (a cad vector3 with x normalX, y normalY and z normalZ) to faceNormals
            set firstWeld to the item at firstIndex in weldOf
            set secondWeld to the item at secondIndex in weldOf
            set thirdWeld to the item at thirdIndex in weldOf
            # A sliver whose corners lie on one line (within rounding) has no
            # direction of its own: it is left out, and the sides of the
            # faces around it meet flush or are drawn as borders.
            set longestSquare to the maximum of ((uX * uX) + ((uY * uY) + (uZ * uZ))) and ((vX * vX) + ((vY * vY) + (vZ * vZ)))
            set wX to vX - uX
            set wY to vY - uY
            set wZ to vZ - uZ
            set longestSquare to the maximum of longestSquare and ((wX * wX) + ((wY * wY) + (wZ * wZ)))
            set solidEnough to magnitude > (0.000000001 * longestSquare)
            set sound to ((firstWeld != secondWeld) and (secondWeld != thirdWeld)) and ((thirdWeld != firstWeld) and solidEnough)
            if sound:
                loop sideCursor from 0 to 3:
                    set fromWeld to firstWeld
                    set toWeld to secondWeld
                    if sideCursor = 1:
                        set fromWeld to secondWeld
                        set toWeld to thirdWeld
                    if sideCursor = 2:
                        set fromWeld to thirdWeld
                        set toWeld to firstWeld
                    set lowWeld to (the minimum of fromWeld and toWeld) as a 64 bit integer
                    set highWeld to (the maximum of fromWeld and toWeld) as a 64 bit integer
                    append ((((lowWeld * keyRoom) + highWeld) * keyRoom) + (triangleCursor as a 64 bit integer)) to sideKeys
        sort and deduplicate bim ids sideKeys
        # Runs of one side key are the faces that share that side.
        set runStart to 0
        set sideCount to the length of sideKeys
        loop while runStart < sideCount:
            set runKey to (the item at runStart in sideKeys) / keyRoom
            set runEnd to runStart + 1
            set scanning to runEnd < sideCount
            loop while scanning:
                if ((the item at runEnd in sideKeys) / keyRoom) = runKey:
                    set runEnd to runEnd + 1
                    set scanning to runEnd < sideCount
                else:
                    set scanning to false
            set lowWeld to (runKey / keyRoom) as an integer
            set highWeld to (the remainder of runKey divided by keyRoom) as an integer
            set drawsEdge to true
            set oneSided to false
            set sideFace to (the remainder of (the item at runStart in sideKeys) divided by keyRoom) as an integer
            if (runEnd - runStart) = 1:
                set oneSided to (the item at sideFace in faceNormals)'s z < -0.000001
            else if (runEnd - runStart) = 2:
                set firstFace to (the remainder of (the item at runStart in sideKeys) divided by keyRoom) as an integer
                set secondFace to (the remainder of (the item at (runStart + 1) in sideKeys) divided by keyRoom) as an integer
                set firstNormal to the item at firstFace in faceNormals
                set secondNormal to the item at secondFace in faceNormals
                set firstToward to firstNormal's z < -0.000001
                set secondToward to secondNormal's z < -0.000001
                set bend to the cad dot of firstNormal and secondNormal
                set folded to false
                if bend < 0.5:
                    set folded to true
                else if bend < 0.99985:
                    # Folded where the mesh stores different normals at the
                    # shared corners; a smooth curve stores the same.
                    set folded to (the length of (meshShape's normals's values)) = 0
                    loop endCursor from 0 to 2:
                        set endWeld to lowWeld
                        if endCursor = 1:
                            set endWeld to highWeld
                        set firstStored to the bim stored normal (the bim corner of triangle firstFace in meshShape welded to endWeld by weldOf) of meshShape on viewPlane deep along depthAxis
                        set secondStored to the bim stored normal (the bim corner of triangle secondFace in meshShape welded to endWeld by weldOf) of meshShape on viewPlane deep along depthAxis
                        if (the cad dot of firstStored and secondStored) < 0.9999:
                            set folded to true
                set drawsEdge to (firstToward or secondToward) and (folded or (firstToward != secondToward))
                if firstToward != secondToward:
                    set oneSided to true
                    set sideFace to firstFace
                    if secondToward:
                        set sideFace to secondFace
            else:
                # More than two faces: solids of one mesh touching (a frame's
                # rails and posts). With one face toward the viewer the side
                # is that face's; with two in one plane on either side of it
                # they continue each other and the side draws nothing; two
                # in one plane on the same side of it (faces lying over each
                # other) give it the first one's.
                set towardTotal to 0
                set firstTowardFace to -1
                set secondTowardFace to -1
                loop faceCursor from runStart to runEnd:
                    set runFace to (the remainder of (the item at faceCursor in sideKeys) divided by keyRoom) as an integer
                    if (the item at runFace in faceNormals)'s z < -0.000001:
                        set towardTotal to towardTotal + 1
                        if firstTowardFace < 0:
                            set firstTowardFace to runFace
                        else:
                            set secondTowardFace to runFace
                if towardTotal = 1:
                    set oneSided to true
                    set sideFace to firstTowardFace
                if towardTotal = 2:
                    if (the cad dot of (the item at firstTowardFace in faceNormals) and (the item at secondTowardFace in faceNormals)) >= (the bim flush alignment):
                        set firstInward to the bim flush inward of face firstTowardFace among indices at viewCorners offset cornerOffset from (the item at lowWeld in weldedCorners) to (the item at highWeld in weldedCorners)
                        set secondInward to the bim flush inward of face secondTowardFace among indices at viewCorners offset cornerOffset from (the item at lowWeld in weldedCorners) to (the item at highWeld in weldedCorners)
                        if (the cad dot of firstInward and secondInward) < -0.5:
                            set drawsEdge to false
                        else:
                            set oneSided to true
                            set sideFace to firstTowardFace
            if drawsEdge:
                set fromCorner to the item at lowWeld in weldedCorners
                set toCorner to the item at highWeld in weldedCorners
                set sideNormal to a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
                set sideInward to sideNormal
                set sideFinish to the string form of ""
                if oneSided:
                    set sideNormal to the item at sideFace in faceNormals
                    set sideInward to the bim flush inward of face sideFace among indices at viewCorners offset cornerOffset from fromCorner to toCorner
                    set sideFinish to the bim finish of face sideFace in meshEntry
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim projection stroke record, meshEntry's elementId, fromCorner, toCorner, oneSided, meshNumber, sideFinish, sideNormal, sideInward)) to candidateEdges
            set runStart to runEnd
        free cornerKeys
        free sortedKeys
        free weldOf
        free weldedCorners
        free faceNormals
        free sideKeys

# The turn the flush hash gives every line before it keys its angle, so
# that the angles 0 and pi, where a line's key changes ends, fall on no
# usual direction (any odd angle will do), and half a turn.
local function the bim flush turn:
    replacement:
        0.4142135623730951
local function the bim half turn:
    replacement:
        3.141592653589793

# The line through `fromCorner` and `toCorner` (drawing coordinates) as the
# flush hash keys it: its angle turned by `the bim flush turn`, from 0 to
# pi (x), and its signed distance from `hashOrigin` (y); x is -1 for a side
# seen end-on.
local function the bim flush line of {cad vector3:fromCorner} to {cad vector3:toCorner} around {cad vector2:hashOrigin}:
    execute:
        set runX to toCorner's x - fromCorner's x
        set runY to toCorner's y - fromCorner's y
        set runLength to the square root of ((runX * runX) + (runY * runY))
        if runLength <= 0.000000001:
            return a cad vector2 with x -1.0 and y 0.0
        set unitX to runX / runLength
        set unitY to runY / runLength
        set turnedX to (unitX * (the cosine of (the bim flush turn))) - (unitY * (the sine of (the bim flush turn)))
        set turnedY to (unitX * (the sine of (the bim flush turn))) + (unitY * (the cosine of (the bim flush turn)))
        if (turnedY < 0.0) or ((turnedY = 0.0) and (turnedX < 0.0)):
            set unitX to 0.0 - unitX
            set unitY to 0.0 - unitY
            set turnedX to 0.0 - turnedX
            set turnedY to 0.0 - turnedY
        set lineAngle to @intrinsic("atan2", turnedY, turnedX)
        return a cad vector2 with x lineAngle and y (((fromCorner's y - hashOrigin's y) * unitX) - ((fromCorner's x - hashOrigin's x) * unitY))

local function the bim flush angle bin of {a 64 bit floating-point number:lineAngle}:
    execute:
        return (the floor of (lineAngle / (the bim flush angle bin))) as a 64 bit integer

local function the bim flush offset bin of {a 64 bit floating-point number:lineOffset}:
    execute:
        set halfRoom to ((the bim flush offset room) / 2) as a 64 bit floating-point number
        set binned to (the floor of (lineOffset / (the bim flush offset bin))) + halfRoom
        set binned to the maximum of 0.0 and (the minimum of binned and (((the bim flush offset room) - 1) as a 64 bit floating-point number))
        return binned as a 64 bit integer

# The depth bin of `depthValue`, kept below the deep bin.
local function the bim flush depth bin of {a 64 bit floating-point number:depthValue}:
    execute:
        set binned to the floor of (depthValue / (the bim flush depth bin))
        set binned to the maximum of -1000000000000.0 and (the minimum of binned and 1000000000000.0)
        return binned as a 64 bit integer

# The line key of an angle bin, a depth bin and an offset bin: the angle
# and depth hashed (two lines that share a hash only cost a comparison),
# the offset below them, so that the keys of neighbouring offsets follow
# each other.
local function the bim flush key of angle bin {a 64 bit integer:angleBin} depth bin {a 64 bit integer:depthBin} and offset bin {a 64 bit integer:offsetBin}:
    execute:
        set hashRoom to (the bim flush hash room) as a 64 bit integer
        set mixed to the remainder of ((angleBin * (40503 as a 64 bit integer)) + (depthBin * (9973 as a 64 bit integer))) divided by hashRoom
        if mixed < (0 as a 64 bit integer):
            set mixed to mixed + hashRoom
        return (mixed * ((the bim flush offset room) as a 64 bit integer)) + offsetBin

# The first position in the ascending `sortedKeys` whose key is at least
# `wanted` (the length when none is).
local function the bim first slot at least {a 64 bit integer:wanted} among {a pointer to a list:sortedKeys}:
    execute:
        set lowSlot to 0
        set highSlot to the length of sortedKeys
        loop while lowSlot < highSlot:
            set middleSlot to (lowSlot + highSlot) / 2
            if (the item at middleSlot in sortedKeys) < wanted:
                set lowSlot to middleSlot + 1
            else:
                set highSlot to middleSlot
        return lowSlot

# The flush hash of `candidateEdges`: for each one-sided edge, in each
# depth bin its ends reach (in the deep bin when they reach through more
# than `the bim flush depth reach`), its line's key times `the bim
# projection key room` plus its position, ascending. Two edges on one line
# in the drawing but at different depths fall in different bins, so each
# edge meets only the few that lie on nearly its line in space.
local function the bim flush keys of {a pointer to a list:candidateEdges} around {cad vector2:hashOrigin}:
    execute:
        set keyRoom to (the bim projection key room) as a 64 bit integer
        set oneBin to 1 as a 64 bit integer
        set flushKeys to an empty list of a 64 bit integer
        set keyedTotal to the minimum of (the length of candidateEdges) and (the bim projection key room)
        loop candidateCursor from 0 to keyedTotal:
            set candidateEdge to the item at candidateCursor in candidateEdges
            if candidateEdge's oneSided:
                set lineSpot to the bim flush line of (candidateEdge's fromCorner) to (candidateEdge's toCorner) around hashOrigin
                if lineSpot's x >= 0.0:
                    set angleBin to the bim flush angle bin of lineSpot's x
                    set offsetBin to the bim flush offset bin of lineSpot's y
                    set lowDepth to the bim flush depth bin of (the minimum of candidateEdge's fromCorner's z and candidateEdge's toCorner's z)
                    set highDepth to the bim flush depth bin of (the maximum of candidateEdge's fromCorner's z and candidateEdge's toCorner's z)
                    if (highDepth - lowDepth) >= ((the bim flush depth reach) as a 64 bit integer):
                        set lowDepth to (the bim flush deep bin) as a 64 bit integer
                        set highDepth to lowDepth
                    set depthCursor to lowDepth
                    loop while depthCursor <= highDepth:
                        set lineKey to the bim flush key of angle bin angleBin depth bin depthCursor and offset bin offsetBin
                        append ((lineKey * keyRoom) + (candidateCursor as a 64 bit integer)) to flushKeys
                        set depthCursor to depthCursor + oneBin
        sort and deduplicate bim ids flushKeys
        return flushKeys

# Takes out of the pieces (parameters along `candidateEdge`, one-sided)
# the stretch where `partner` continues its face flush: the partnerEdge's face
# looks the same way, in the same plane, from the other side of the same
# line, and is of the same mesh or shows the same finish.
local function take bim flush stretch of {bim projection stroke record:candidateEdge} against {bim projection stroke record:partnerEdge} out of {a pointer to a list:pieceStarts} and {a pointer to a list:pieceEnds}:
    execute:
        set sameMesh to candidateEdge's meshNumber = partnerEdge's meshNumber
        set sameFinish to (candidateEdge's finishName != (the string form of "")) and (candidateEdge's finishName = partnerEdge's finishName)
        if (sameMesh = false) and (sameFinish = false):
            return nothing
        if (the cad dot of (candidateEdge's normal) and (partnerEdge's normal)) < (the bim flush alignment):
            return nothing
        if (the cad dot of (candidateEdge's inward) and (partnerEdge's inward)) > -0.5:
            return nothing
        set runVector to the cad difference of (candidateEdge's toCorner) and (candidateEdge's fromCorner)
        set runSquare to the cad dot of runVector and runVector
        if runSquare <= 0.0:
            return nothing
        set fromParameter to (the cad dot of (the cad difference of (partnerEdge's fromCorner) and (candidateEdge's fromCorner)) and runVector) / runSquare
        set toParameter to (the cad dot of (the cad difference of (partnerEdge's toCorner) and (candidateEdge's fromCorner)) and runVector) / runSquare
        set fromGap to the cad length of (the cad difference of (partnerEdge's fromCorner) and (the cad sum of (candidateEdge's fromCorner) and (runVector scaled by fromParameter)))
        set toGap to the cad length of (the cad difference of (partnerEdge's toCorner) and (the cad sum of (candidateEdge's fromCorner) and (runVector scaled by toParameter)))
        if (fromGap > (the bim flush tolerance)) or (toGap > (the bim flush tolerance)):
            return nothing
        take bim stretch (the minimum of fromParameter and toParameter) until (the maximum of fromParameter and toParameter) out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds

# Takes out of the pieces of edge `candidateIndex` what the one-sided
# edges keyed `angleBin`, `depthBin` and an offset bin from `offsetBin` - 1
# to `offsetBin` + 1 continue flush; their keys follow each other.
local function take bim flush matches spanning {integer:candidateIndex} among {a pointer to a list:candidateEdges} keyed by {a pointer to a list:flushKeys} at {a 64 bit integer:angleBin} deep {a 64 bit integer:depthBin} and {a 64 bit integer:offsetBin} out of {a pointer to a list:pieceStarts} and {a pointer to a list:pieceEnds}:
    execute:
        set noBin to 0 as a 64 bit integer
        set oneBin to 1 as a 64 bit integer
        if angleBin < noBin:
            return nothing
        set keyRoom to (the bim projection key room) as a 64 bit integer
        set lowKey to the bim flush key of angle bin angleBin depth bin depthBin and offset bin (the maximum of noBin and (offsetBin - oneBin))
        set highKey to the bim flush key of angle bin angleBin depth bin depthBin and offset bin (the minimum of (offsetBin + oneBin) and (((the bim flush offset room) as a 64 bit integer) - oneBin))
        set keySlot to the bim first slot at least (lowKey * keyRoom) among flushKeys
        set candidateEdge to the item at candidateIndex in candidateEdges
        set scanning to keySlot < (the length of flushKeys)
        loop while scanning:
            set entryKey to the item at keySlot in flushKeys
            if (entryKey / keyRoom) > highKey:
                set scanning to false
            else:
                set partnerIndex to (the remainder of entryKey divided by keyRoom) as an integer
                if partnerIndex != candidateIndex:
                    take bim flush stretch of candidateEdge against (the item at partnerIndex in candidateEdges) out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds
                set keySlot to keySlot + 1
                set scanning to keySlot < (the length of flushKeys)

# Takes out of the pieces of one-sided edge `candidateIndex` every
# stretch that another one-sided edge continues flush: those keyed in the
# angle and offset bins around its line's, in each depth bin its ends reach
# (within the tolerance) and in the deep bin, and, for a line keyed near
# angle 0 or pi, those keyed near the other end with the offset turned
# over.
local function take bim flush stretches spanning {integer:candidateIndex} among {a pointer to a list:candidateEdges} keyed by {a pointer to a list:flushKeys} around {cad vector2:hashOrigin} out of {a pointer to a list:pieceStarts} and {a pointer to a list:pieceEnds}:
    execute:
        set candidateEdge to the item at candidateIndex in candidateEdges
        set lineSpot to the bim flush line of (candidateEdge's fromCorner) to (candidateEdge's toCorner) around hashOrigin
        if lineSpot's x < 0.0:
            return nothing
        set angleBin to the bim flush angle bin of lineSpot's x
        set offsetBin to the bim flush offset bin of lineSpot's y
        set mirroredBin to the bim flush offset bin of (0.0 - lineSpot's y)
        set lastBin to the bim flush angle bin of (the bim half turn)
        set oneBin to 1 as a 64 bit integer
        set nearEnd to (angleBin <= oneBin) or (angleBin >= (lastBin - oneBin))
        set otherBin to lastBin
        if angleBin >= (lastBin - oneBin):
            set otherBin to 0 as a 64 bit integer
        set deepBin to (the bim flush deep bin) as a 64 bit integer
        set lowDepth to the bim flush depth bin of ((the minimum of candidateEdge's fromCorner's z and candidateEdge's toCorner's z) - (the bim flush tolerance))
        set highDepth to the bim flush depth bin of ((the maximum of candidateEdge's fromCorner's z and candidateEdge's toCorner's z) + (the bim flush tolerance))
        set depthCursor to lowDepth
        set searching to true
        loop while searching:
            loop angleStep from 0 to 3:
                take bim flush matches spanning candidateIndex among candidateEdges keyed by flushKeys at ((angleBin + (angleStep as a 64 bit integer)) - oneBin) deep depthCursor and offsetBin out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds
                if nearEnd:
                    take bim flush matches spanning candidateIndex among candidateEdges keyed by flushKeys at ((otherBin + (angleStep as a 64 bit integer)) - oneBin) deep depthCursor and mirroredBin out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds
            if depthCursor = deepBin:
                set searching to false
            else if depthCursor >= highDepth:
                set depthCursor to deepBin
            else:
                set depthCursor to depthCursor + oneBin

# The point the flush hash keys the offsets of lines from (drawing
# coordinates): the first corner of the first outlined mesh, rounded to
# the nearest point of `the bim flush origin grid`, so that a model far
# from its origin keeps its lines apart, and so that it stays put while
# elements are edited (rounded to the nearest, a model about its origin
# keeps the origin, rather than flipping between two points of the grid
# when a corner crosses 0): a
# projection worked out again in part (`update bim kept projection`) keys
# its edges as the whole one did, and two edges are found flush or not
# alike in both.
local function the bim flush origin of {a pointer to a list:meshList} on {cad plane:viewPlane} deep along {cad vector3:depthAxis}:
    execute:
        set originGrid to the bim flush origin grid
        loop meshCursor from 0 to the length of meshList:
            set projectionMesh to the item at meshCursor in meshList
            if (projectionMesh's outlined) and ((the length of (projectionMesh's shape's positions's values)) > 0):
                set firstCorner to the bim view coordinates of (the item at 0 in (projectionMesh's shape's positions's values)) on viewPlane deep along depthAxis
                return a cad vector2 with x ((the floor of ((firstCorner's x / originGrid) + 0.5)) * originGrid) and y ((the floor of ((firstCorner's y / originGrid) + 0.5)) * originGrid)
        return a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0

# The visible edges of `meshes` (`bim projection mesh record`s) seen square
# onto `viewPlane`, in drawing coordinates: within the drawing's width from
# `lowAlong` to `highAlong`, beyond the plane up to `depthLimit` (no limit
# when it is 0 or less), hidden by every mesh in front and by the cut
# polygons of `cutView`, which lie on the plane.
function the bim projected edges of {a pointer to a list:meshes} on {cad plane:viewPlane} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowAlong} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:highAlong} within {a 64 bit floating-point number:depthLimit} behind {bim view record:cutView}:
    execute:
        set meshEdgeCounts to an empty list of an integer
        set result to the bim projected edges of meshes on viewPlane from lowAlong to highAlong within depthLimit behind cutView counting meshEdgeCounts
        free meshEdgeCounts
        return result

# The same, appending to `meshEdgeCounts` how many of the edges each mesh
# drew: the edges come mesh after mesh, in the meshes' order.
function the bim projected edges of {a pointer to a list:meshes} on {cad plane:viewPlane} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowAlong} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:highAlong} within {a 64 bit floating-point number:depthLimit} behind {bim view record:cutView} counting {a pointer to a list:meshEdgeCounts}:
    execute:
        set hashOrigin to the bim flush origin of meshes on viewPlane deep along (the bim depth axis of viewPlane)
        set everyMeshDraws to an empty list of an integer
        set result to the bim projected edges of meshes on viewPlane from lowAlong to highAlong within depthLimit behind cutView keyed around hashOrigin drawing everyMeshDraws counting meshEdgeCounts
        free everyMeshDraws
        return result

# The same, with the flush hash keyed around `hashOrigin`, and drawing the
# edges only of the meshes whose flag in `drawFlags` is 1 (of every
# outlined mesh when it is empty): the edges of the other outlined meshes
# that name finishes are only looked at as flush partners of those drawn,
# and they count 0. One without finishes can be no other mesh's partner
# (see `take bim flush stretch of`), so its edges are not worked out.
local function the bim projected edges of {a pointer to a list:meshes} on {cad plane:viewPlane} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowAlong} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:highAlong} within {a 64 bit floating-point number:depthLimit} behind {bim view record:cutView} keyed around {cad vector2:hashOrigin} drawing {a pointer to a list:drawFlags} counting {a pointer to a list:meshEdgeCounts}:
    execute:
        set result to a cad topology list of a bim projected edge record
        set depthAxis to the bim depth axis of viewPlane
        set farDepth to 1e300
        if depthLimit > 0.0:
            set farDepth to depthLimit
        set occluders to @intrinsic("construct", a bim projection occluders record, a cad topology list of a cad vector3, a cad topology list of a cad vector2, a cad topology list of a cad vector2, a cad topology list of a 64 bit floating-point number, a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1, 1, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer)
        # Every mesh's corners in drawing coordinates and depth, once, one
        # mesh after another from its offset.
        set viewCorners to an empty list of a cad vector3
        set cornerOffsets to an empty list of an integer
        loop meshCursor from 0 to the length of meshes:
            set projectionMesh to the item at meshCursor in meshes
            set cornerOffset to the length of viewCorners
            append cornerOffset to cornerOffsets
            loop cornerCursor from 0 to the length of (projectionMesh's shape's positions's values):
                append (the bim view coordinates of (the item at cornerCursor in (projectionMesh's shape's positions's values)) on viewPlane deep along depthAxis) to viewCorners
            add bim occluders of projectionMesh's shape at viewCorners offset cornerOffset from lowAlong to highAlong until farDepth into occluders
        index bim occluders (the address of occluders)
        # The edges of every outlined mesh, less the stretches that a face
        # beyond them continues flush, cut by what lies in front.
        set everyOneDraws to (the length of drawFlags) = 0
        set candidateEdges to an empty list of a bim projection stroke record
        set drawnCounts to an empty list of an integer
        loop meshCursor from 0 to the length of meshes:
            set projectionMesh to the item at meshCursor in meshes
            append 0 to drawnCounts
            set givesEdges to everyOneDraws
            if everyOneDraws = false:
                set givesEdges to ((the item at meshCursor in drawFlags) = 1) or ((the length of (projectionMesh's finishes's values)) > 0)
            if (projectionMesh's outlined) and givesEdges:
                set cornerOffset to the item at meshCursor in cornerOffsets
                append bim drawn edges of projectionMesh numbered meshCursor at viewCorners offset cornerOffset counted (the length of (projectionMesh's shape's positions's values)) on viewPlane deep along depthAxis into candidateEdges
        set flushKeys to the bim flush keys of candidateEdges around hashOrigin
        set edgeNumber to 0 as a 64 bit integer
        set pieceStarts to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        set pieceEnds to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        loop candidateCursor from 0 to the length of candidateEdges:
            set candidateEdge to the item at candidateCursor in candidateEdges
            set candidateDraws to everyOneDraws
            if everyOneDraws = false:
                set candidateDraws to (the item at candidateEdge's meshNumber in drawFlags) = 1
            if candidateDraws:
                set edgesBefore to the length of (result's values)
                clear pieceStarts
                clear pieceEnds
                append 0.0 to pieceStarts
                append 1.0 to pieceEnds
                if candidateEdge's oneSided:
                    take bim flush stretches spanning candidateCursor among candidateEdges keyed by flushKeys around hashOrigin out of pieceStarts and pieceEnds
                set runVector to the cad difference of (candidateEdge's toCorner) and (candidateEdge's fromCorner)
                loop pieceCursor from 0 to the length of pieceStarts:
                    set pieceStart to the item at pieceCursor in pieceStarts
                    set pieceEnd to the item at pieceCursor in pieceEnds
                    set stretchStart to candidateEdge's fromCorner
                    set stretchEnd to candidateEdge's toCorner
                    if pieceStart > 0.0:
                        set stretchStart to the cad sum of (candidateEdge's fromCorner) and (runVector scaled by pieceStart)
                    if pieceEnd < 1.0:
                        set stretchEnd to the cad sum of (candidateEdge's fromCorner) and (runVector scaled by pieceEnd)
                    set edgeNumber to edgeNumber + (1 as a 64 bit integer)
                    append bim visible pieces of edge stretchStart till stretchEnd for element (candidateEdge's elementId) numbered edgeNumber between lowAlong and highAlong until farDepth among occluders behind cutView into (result's values)
                # The candidates come mesh after mesh, so the edges do too.
                set meshSlot to candidateEdge's meshNumber
                replace item at index meshSlot in drawnCounts with ((the item at meshSlot in drawnCounts) + ((the length of (result's values)) - edgesBefore))
        loop meshCursor from 0 to the length of drawnCounts:
            append (the item at meshCursor in drawnCounts) to meshEdgeCounts
        free viewCorners
        free cornerOffsets
        free candidateEdges
        free drawnCounts
        free flushKeys
        free pieceStarts
        free pieceEnds
        return result

# ---------------------------------------------------- kept while editing

# A projection kept from one frame to the next, so that a continuous edit
# (a drag) works out again only the edges it can have changed: the meshes
# and the cut the edges were worked out from (the cut copied, so that a
# view updated in place cannot change it unseen), each mesh's box in the
# drawing, how many of `edges` (mesh after mesh) each drew, the plane and
# limits, and the origin the flush hash keyed the edges around. The meshes are kept as given: whoever makes them makes new
# triangles for a changed element rather than changing the old ones in
# place (the evaluation's tessellation and the scene's meshes do).
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim kept projection record
    members:
        valid as a boolean
        viewPlane as a cad plane
        lowAlong as a 64 bit floating-point number
        highAlong as a 64 bit floating-point number
        depthLimit as a 64 bit floating-point number
        hashOrigin as a cad vector2
        meshes as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim projection mesh record)
        lows as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector2)
        highs as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector2)
        counts as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        sources as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim cut source record)
        edges as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim projected edge record)
        # How many meshes the last update worked the edges of out, whether
        # it updated the edges kept rather than working them all out, and
        # the elements of the meshes it worked out, for tests and timing.
        redrawn as an integer
        partial as a boolean
        redrawnIds as the type of (a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer)

function an empty bim kept projection:
    execute:
        return @intrinsic("construct", a bim kept projection record, false, (a cad plane with origin (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0), x axis (the cad x axis) and y axis (the cad y axis)), 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0, a cad topology list of a bim projection mesh record, a cad topology list of a cad vector2, a cad topology list of a cad vector2, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of a bim cut source record, a cad topology list of a bim projected edge record, 0, false, a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer)

# How far apart in the drawing (metres) two boxes may lie and still be
# taken to touch: more than the tolerances by which a triangle or a cut
# polygon hides what lies just outside its outline.
local function the bim projection box slack:
    replacement:
        0.001

# Whether the box from `lowCorner` to `highCorner` and the box from
# `otherLow` to `otherHigh` touch, within the box slack.
local function bim box {cad vector2:lowCorner} till {cad vector2:highCorner} touches {cad vector2:otherLow} through {cad vector2:otherHigh}:
    execute:
        set boxSlack to the bim projection box slack
        set acrossX to ((lowCorner's x - boxSlack) <= otherHigh's x) and ((otherLow's x - boxSlack) <= highCorner's x)
        set acrossY to ((lowCorner's y - boxSlack) <= otherHigh's y) and ((otherLow's y - boxSlack) <= highCorner's y)
        return acrossX and acrossY

# Whether the box from `lowCorner` to `highCorner` touches one of the boxes
# from `otherLows` to `otherHighs`.
local function bim box {cad vector2:lowCorner} till {cad vector2:highCorner} meets one of {a pointer to a list:otherLows} and {a pointer to a list:otherHighs}:
    execute:
        loop boxCursor from 0 to the length of otherLows:
            if bim box lowCorner till highCorner touches (the item at boxCursor in otherLows) through (the item at boxCursor in otherHighs):
                return true
        return false

# The box in the drawing of the corners of `meshShape`, appended to
# `boxLows` and `boxHighs` (an empty mesh's box touches nothing).
local function append bim drawing box of {fast mesh record:meshShape} on {cad plane:viewPlane} deep along {cad vector3:depthAxis} to {a pointer to a list:boxLows} and {a pointer to a list:boxHighs}:
    execute:
        set lowX to 1e300
        set lowY to 1e300
        set highX to -1e300
        set highY to -1e300
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to the length of (meshShape's positions's values):
            set viewCorner to the bim view coordinates of (the item at cornerCursor in (meshShape's positions's values)) on viewPlane deep along depthAxis
            set lowX to the minimum of lowX and viewCorner's x
            set lowY to the minimum of lowY and viewCorner's y
            set highX to the maximum of highX and viewCorner's x
            set highY to the maximum of highY and viewCorner's y
        append (a cad vector2 with x lowX and y lowY) to boxLows
        append (a cad vector2 with x highX and y highY) to boxHighs

# The box of the cut polygons of `cutSource` (drawing coordinates),
# appended to `boxLows` and `boxHighs`.
local function append bim cut box of {bim cut source record:cutSource} to {a pointer to a list:boxLows} and {a pointer to a list:boxHighs}:
    execute:
        set lowX to 1e300
        set lowY to 1e300
        set highX to -1e300
        set highY to -1e300
        loop polygonCursor from 0 to the length of (cutSource's polygons's values):
            set cutRing to (the item at polygonCursor in (cutSource's polygons's values))'s points's values
            loop cornerCursor from 0 to the length of cutRing:
                set ringCorner to the item at cornerCursor in cutRing
                set lowX to the minimum of lowX and ringCorner's x
                set lowY to the minimum of lowY and ringCorner's y
                set highX to the maximum of highX and ringCorner's x
                set highY to the maximum of highY and ringCorner's y
        append (a cad vector2 with x lowX and y lowY) to boxLows
        append (a cad vector2 with x highX and y highY) to boxHighs

# Whether projection meshes `keptMesh` and `freshMesh` are the same: one
# element, drawn alike, with the same finishes on the same faces (which
# decide what meets it flush), and the same corners, normals and
# triangles.
local function bim projection mesh {bim projection mesh record:keptMesh} matches {bim projection mesh record:freshMesh}:
    execute:
        if (keptMesh's elementId != freshMesh's elementId) or (keptMesh's outlined != freshMesh's outlined):
            return false
        set keptFinishes to keptMesh's finishes's values
        set freshFinishes to freshMesh's finishes's values
        if (the length of keptFinishes) != (the length of freshFinishes):
            return false
        loop finishCursor from 0 to the length of keptFinishes:
            if (the item at finishCursor in keptFinishes) != (the item at finishCursor in freshFinishes):
                return false
        set keptFaceFinishes to keptMesh's faceFinishes's values
        set freshFaceFinishes to freshMesh's faceFinishes's values
        if (the length of keptFaceFinishes) != (the length of freshFaceFinishes):
            return false
        loop faceCursor from 0 to the length of keptFaceFinishes:
            if (the item at faceCursor in keptFaceFinishes) != (the item at faceCursor in freshFaceFinishes):
                return false
        set keptPositions to keptMesh's shape's positions's values
        set freshPositions to freshMesh's shape's positions's values
        set keptNormals to keptMesh's shape's normals's values
        set freshNormals to freshMesh's shape's normals's values
        set keptIndices to keptMesh's shape's triangles's values
        set freshIndices to freshMesh's shape's triangles's values
        if (the length of keptPositions) != (the length of freshPositions):
            return false
        if (the length of keptNormals) != (the length of freshNormals):
            return false
        if (the length of keptIndices) != (the length of freshIndices):
            return false
        loop cornerCursor from 0 to the length of keptPositions:
            set keptCorner to the item at cornerCursor in keptPositions
            set freshCorner to the item at cornerCursor in freshPositions
            if ((keptCorner's x != freshCorner's x) or (keptCorner's y != freshCorner's y)) or (keptCorner's z != freshCorner's z):
                return false
        loop normalCursor from 0 to the length of keptNormals:
            set keptNormal to the item at normalCursor in keptNormals
            set freshNormal to the item at normalCursor in freshNormals
            if ((keptNormal's x != freshNormal's x) or (keptNormal's y != freshNormal's y)) or (keptNormal's z != freshNormal's z):
                return false
        loop indexCursor from 0 to the length of keptIndices:
            if (the item at indexCursor in keptIndices) != (the item at indexCursor in freshIndices):
                return false
        return true

# Whether cut sources `keptSource` and `freshSource` cut the same: one
# element, with the same polygons.
local function bim cut source {bim cut source record:keptSource} matches {bim cut source record:freshSource}:
    execute:
        if keptSource's id != freshSource's id:
            return false
        set keptPolygons to keptSource's polygons's values
        set freshPolygons to freshSource's polygons's values
        if (the length of keptPolygons) != (the length of freshPolygons):
            return false
        loop polygonCursor from 0 to the length of keptPolygons:
            set keptRing to (the item at polygonCursor in keptPolygons)'s points's values
            set freshRing to (the item at polygonCursor in freshPolygons)'s points's values
            if (the length of keptRing) != (the length of freshRing):
                return false
            loop cornerCursor from 0 to the length of keptRing:
                set keptCorner to the item at cornerCursor in keptRing
                set freshCorner to the item at cornerCursor in freshRing
                if (keptCorner's x != freshCorner's x) or (keptCorner's y != freshCorner's y):
                    return false
        return true

# A copy of the cut sources `sourceList`, down to their polygons' corners.
local function the bim copied cut sources of {a pointer to a list:sourceList}:
    execute:
        set sourceCopies to a cad topology list of a bim cut source record
        loop sourceCursor from 0 to the length of sourceList:
            set givenSource to the item at sourceCursor in sourceList
            set sourceCopy to @intrinsic("construct", a bim cut source record, givenSource's id, givenSource's serial, givenSource's refused, a cad topology list of a bim cut polygon record)
            loop polygonCursor from 0 to the length of (givenSource's polygons's values):
                set polygonValue to the item at polygonCursor in (givenSource's polygons's values)
                set cornerCopies to a cad topology list of a cad vector2
                loop cornerCursor from 0 to the length of (polygonValue's points's values):
                    append (the item at cornerCursor in (polygonValue's points's values)) to (cornerCopies's values)
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim cut polygon record, polygonValue's elementId, cornerCopies)) to (sourceCopy's polygons's values)
            append sourceCopy to (sourceCopies's values)
        return sourceCopies

# Works the edges of `meshList` out whole, as `the bim projected edges of
# … on …` does, into `keptHolder`, keeping what they were worked out from.
function project bim kept projection {a pointer to a bim kept projection record:keptHolder} of {a pointer to a list:meshList} on {cad plane:viewPlane} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowAlong} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:highAlong} within {a 64 bit floating-point number:depthLimit} behind {bim view record:cutView}:
    execute:
        set depthAxis to the bim depth axis of viewPlane
        set freshCounts to a cad topology list of an integer
        set freshOrigin to the bim flush origin of meshList on viewPlane deep along depthAxis
        set everyMeshDraws to an empty list of an integer
        set keptHolder's edges to the bim projected edges of meshList on viewPlane from lowAlong to highAlong within depthLimit behind cutView keyed around freshOrigin drawing everyMeshDraws counting (freshCounts's values)
        free everyMeshDraws
        set freshMeshes to a cad topology list of a bim projection mesh record
        set freshLows to a cad topology list of a cad vector2
        set freshHighs to a cad topology list of a cad vector2
        set outlinedTotal to 0
        set outlinedIds to a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer
        loop meshCursor from 0 to the length of meshList:
            set freshMesh to the item at meshCursor in meshList
            append freshMesh to (freshMeshes's values)
            append bim drawing box of freshMesh's shape on viewPlane deep along depthAxis to (freshLows's values) and (freshHighs's values)
            if freshMesh's outlined:
                set outlinedTotal to outlinedTotal + 1
                append freshMesh's elementId to (outlinedIds's values)
        set keptHolder's valid to true
        set keptHolder's viewPlane to viewPlane
        set keptHolder's lowAlong to lowAlong
        set keptHolder's highAlong to highAlong
        set keptHolder's depthLimit to depthLimit
        set keptHolder's hashOrigin to freshOrigin
        set keptHolder's meshes to freshMeshes
        set keptHolder's lows to freshLows
        set keptHolder's highs to freshHighs
        set keptHolder's counts to freshCounts
        set keptHolder's sources to the bim copied cut sources of (cutView's sources's values)
        set keptHolder's redrawn to outlinedTotal
        set keptHolder's partial to false
        set keptHolder's redrawnIds to outlinedIds

# Brings the edges `keptHolder` keeps up to `meshList` cut by `cutView`, as
# `project bim kept projection` would work them out whole, working out
# again only the edges of the meshes that may have changed: each mesh not
# found unchanged among those kept (by element, in order, corner for
# corner), and each mesh whose box in the drawing touches the box of a mesh
# or cut polygon changed, added or gone. A mesh's edges depend only on its
# own triangles, on the triangles whose boxes touch theirs, on the cut
# polygons whose boxes touch theirs and on the edges of the outlined meshes
# whose boxes touch theirs, which may continue them flush (a flush partner
# lies on the same line, within the flush tolerance of a tenth of the box
# slack, and shares a stretch of it with the edge: one that only touches
# its end takes nothing away), so the edges of every other mesh are kept as
# they were. The meshes worked out again are hidden only by the meshes and
# cut polygons that touch them, and are continued flush only by the edges
# of the outlined meshes that touch them: those are worked out with them,
# as partners, but not drawn again. The flush hash is keyed around the same
# origin as the whole projection's, so that each pair of edges is found
# flush or not alike. Worked out whole when nothing is kept, when the
# plane or its limits differ, or when that origin moves.
function update bim kept projection {a pointer to a bim kept projection record:keptHolder} with {a pointer to a list:meshList} on {cad plane:viewPlane} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowAlong} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:highAlong} within {a 64 bit floating-point number:depthLimit} behind {bim view record:cutView}:
    execute:
        set sameFrame to (keptHolder's valid) and (bim planes keptHolder's viewPlane and viewPlane are identical)
        set sameLimits to ((keptHolder's lowAlong = lowAlong) and (keptHolder's highAlong = highAlong)) and (keptHolder's depthLimit = depthLimit)
        if (sameFrame and sameLimits) = false:
            project bim kept projection keptHolder of meshList on viewPlane from lowAlong to highAlong within depthLimit behind cutView
            return nothing
        set depthAxis to the bim depth axis of viewPlane
        set freshOrigin to the bim flush origin of meshList on viewPlane deep along depthAxis
        if (freshOrigin's x != keptHolder's hashOrigin's x) or (freshOrigin's y != keptHolder's hashOrigin's y):
            project bim kept projection keptHolder of meshList on viewPlane from lowAlong to highAlong within depthLimit behind cutView
            return nothing
        set meshTotal to the length of meshList
        set freshLows to a cad topology list of a cad vector2
        set freshHighs to a cad topology list of a cad vector2
        loop meshCursor from 0 to meshTotal:
            append bim drawing box of (the item at meshCursor in meshList)'s shape on viewPlane deep along depthAxis to (freshLows's values) and (freshHighs's values)
        # Each mesh found among those kept, in order; what is not found, and
        # what was kept and is not found again, changed.
        set keptMeshes to keptHolder's meshes's values
        set keptTotal to the length of keptMeshes
        set keptFound to an empty list of an integer
        loop keptCursor from 0 to keptTotal:
            append 0 to keptFound
        set matchOf to an empty list of an integer
        set changedLows to an empty list of a cad vector2
        set changedHighs to an empty list of a cad vector2
        set keptFrom to 0
        loop meshCursor from 0 to meshTotal:
            set freshMesh to the item at meshCursor in meshList
            set foundSlot to -1
            set seekSlot to keptFrom
            loop while (foundSlot < 0) and (seekSlot < keptTotal):
                if bim projection mesh (the item at seekSlot in keptMeshes) matches freshMesh:
                    set foundSlot to seekSlot
                set seekSlot to seekSlot + 1
            append foundSlot to matchOf
            if foundSlot >= 0:
                replace item at index foundSlot in keptFound with 1
                set keptFrom to foundSlot + 1
            else:
                append (the item at meshCursor in (freshLows's values)) to changedLows
                append (the item at meshCursor in (freshHighs's values)) to changedHighs
        loop keptCursor from 0 to keptTotal:
            if (the item at keptCursor in keptFound) = 0:
                append (the item at keptCursor in (keptHolder's lows's values)) to changedLows
                append (the item at keptCursor in (keptHolder's highs's values)) to changedHighs
        # The cut polygons the same way.
        set freshSources to the bim copied cut sources of (cutView's sources's values)
        set keptSources to keptHolder's sources's values
        set keptSourceTotal to the length of keptSources
        set sourceFound to an empty list of an integer
        loop keptCursor from 0 to keptSourceTotal:
            append 0 to sourceFound
        set keptFrom to 0
        loop sourceCursor from 0 to the length of (freshSources's values):
            set freshSource to the item at sourceCursor in (freshSources's values)
            set foundSlot to -1
            set seekSlot to keptFrom
            loop while (foundSlot < 0) and (seekSlot < keptSourceTotal):
                if bim cut source (the item at seekSlot in keptSources) matches freshSource:
                    set foundSlot to seekSlot
                set seekSlot to seekSlot + 1
            if foundSlot >= 0:
                replace item at index foundSlot in sourceFound with 1
                set keptFrom to foundSlot + 1
            else:
                append bim cut box of freshSource to changedLows and changedHighs
        loop keptCursor from 0 to keptSourceTotal:
            if (the item at keptCursor in sourceFound) = 0:
                append bim cut box of (the item at keptCursor in keptSources) to changedLows and changedHighs
        # The outlined meshes whose edges are worked out again, and their
        # boxes.
        set redrawFlags to an empty list of an integer
        set redrawnIds to a cad topology list of a 64 bit integer
        set redrawnLows to an empty list of a cad vector2
        set redrawnHighs to an empty list of a cad vector2
        loop meshCursor from 0 to meshTotal:
            set freshMesh to the item at meshCursor in meshList
            set meshLow to the item at meshCursor in (freshLows's values)
            set meshHigh to the item at meshCursor in (freshHighs's values)
            set redraws to false
            if freshMesh's outlined:
                if (the item at meshCursor in matchOf) < 0:
                    set redraws to true
                else if bim box meshLow till meshHigh meets one of changedLows and changedHighs:
                    set redraws to true
            if redraws:
                append 1 to redrawFlags
                append freshMesh's elementId to (redrawnIds's values)
                append meshLow to redrawnLows
                append meshHigh to redrawnHighs
            else:
                append 0 to redrawFlags
        # Those worked out among the meshes and cut polygons that touch them:
        # the others hide as they do, and those outlined lend their edges
        # as flush partners, but none of them is drawn.
        set partialSlots to an empty list of an integer
        set partialEdges to a cad topology list of a bim projected edge record
        set partialCounts to an empty list of an integer
        if (the length of redrawnLows) > 0:
            set partialMeshes to an empty list of a bim projection mesh record
            set partialDraws to an empty list of an integer
            loop meshCursor from 0 to meshTotal:
                set freshMesh to the item at meshCursor in meshList
                if bim box (the item at meshCursor in (freshLows's values)) till (the item at meshCursor in (freshHighs's values)) meets one of redrawnLows and redrawnHighs:
                    append (the length of partialMeshes) to partialSlots
                    append freshMesh to partialMeshes
                    append (the item at meshCursor in redrawFlags) to partialDraws
                else:
                    append (0 - 1) to partialSlots
            set partialView to an empty bim view
            set partialView's viewPlane to cutView's viewPlane
            set sourceLows to an empty list of a cad vector2
            set sourceHighs to an empty list of a cad vector2
            loop sourceCursor from 0 to the length of (cutView's sources's values):
                set cutSource to the item at sourceCursor in (cutView's sources's values)
                append bim cut box of cutSource to sourceLows and sourceHighs
                if bim box (the item at sourceCursor in sourceLows) till (the item at sourceCursor in sourceHighs) meets one of redrawnLows and redrawnHighs:
                    append cutSource to (partialView's sources's values)
            set partialEdges to the bim projected edges of partialMeshes on viewPlane from lowAlong to highAlong within depthLimit behind partialView keyed around freshOrigin drawing partialDraws counting partialCounts
            free partialMeshes
            free partialDraws
            free sourceLows
            free sourceHighs
        # The edges in the meshes' order: worked out again, or kept.
        set keptOffsets to an empty list of an integer
        set runningTotal to 0
        loop keptCursor from 0 to the length of (keptHolder's counts's values):
            append runningTotal to keptOffsets
            set runningTotal to runningTotal + (the item at keptCursor in (keptHolder's counts's values))
        set partialOffsets to an empty list of an integer
        set runningTotal to 0
        loop partialCursor from 0 to the length of partialCounts:
            append runningTotal to partialOffsets
            set runningTotal to runningTotal + (the item at partialCursor in partialCounts)
        set mergedEdges to a cad topology list of a bim projected edge record
        set mergedCounts to a cad topology list of an integer
        loop meshCursor from 0 to meshTotal:
            set edgesBefore to the length of (mergedEdges's values)
            if (the item at meshCursor in redrawFlags) = 1:
                # A mesh without corners has an empty box that touches
                # nothing, itself included, so it was not worked out: it
                # draws no edges, as in a projection worked out whole.
                set partialSlot to the item at meshCursor in partialSlots
                if partialSlot >= 0:
                    set firstEdge to the item at partialSlot in partialOffsets
                    loop edgeCursor from firstEdge to (firstEdge + (the item at partialSlot in partialCounts)):
                        append (the item at edgeCursor in (partialEdges's values)) to (mergedEdges's values)
            else if (the item at meshCursor in matchOf) >= 0:
                set keptSlot to the item at meshCursor in matchOf
                set firstEdge to the item at keptSlot in keptOffsets
                loop edgeCursor from firstEdge to (firstEdge + (the item at keptSlot in (keptHolder's counts's values))):
                    append (the item at edgeCursor in (keptHolder's edges's values)) to (mergedEdges's values)
            append ((the length of (mergedEdges's values)) - edgesBefore) to (mergedCounts's values)
        set freshMeshes to a cad topology list of a bim projection mesh record
        loop meshCursor from 0 to meshTotal:
            append (the item at meshCursor in meshList) to (freshMeshes's values)
        set keptHolder's meshes to freshMeshes
        set keptHolder's lows to freshLows
        set keptHolder's highs to freshHighs
        set keptHolder's counts to mergedCounts
        set keptHolder's sources to freshSources
        set keptHolder's edges to mergedEdges
        set keptHolder's redrawn to the length of redrawnLows
        set keptHolder's partial to true
        set keptHolder's redrawnIds to redrawnIds
        free keptFound
        free matchOf
        free changedLows
        free changedHighs
        free sourceFound
        free redrawFlags
        free redrawnLows
        free redrawnHighs
        free partialSlots
        free partialCounts
        free keptOffsets
        free partialOffsets

# The plane an elevation looks along: upright through the line from
# `lineStart` to `lineFinish` in plan, looking to its left, as a section's.
function the bim elevation plane from {cad vector2:lineStart} to {cad vector2:lineFinish}:
    execute:
        return the bim section plane from lineStart to lineFinish
